spec/desig/tasks/requirements i want to ddo a spc fr llm generated ui using sjon-render and  schema from blobs. i am going to paste what i  used to get it working manually. the repos are operation-dashboard-ui-07 and odbus grpc tonic i want the entire gui to be auto generates There are two catalogs and one live stream. They only become a GUI when a spec names catalog types whose props read stream state.

  1. Component catalog (what may be drawn)

  This is the json-render vocabulary in TypeScript: defineCatalog + defineRegistry.

  • Contract: src/json-render/catalog/catalog.ts — Zod props, slots, events, actions (navigate, toggleState, …).
  • Paint: registry.tsx — each name maps to a React El<"name">.
  • Pinned export: schemas/json-render/catalog.schema.json + catalog.prompt.md (sha256 in catalog.manifest.json). Gallery admission (op-gallery-gen CatalogGuard) uses this file, not a restated Rust
    list.
  • Spec wire format: flat { root, elements } where children are keys, not nested objects. The renderer refuses any type not in this catalog.

  Shell chrome (appShell, navItem, …) and page widgets (card, stateValue, antigravityChatContainer, named stream objects, …) all live here. NAV_MANIFEST + PAGE_SPECS compose those names into screens.

  catalog.prompt() teaches JSONL RFC-6902 patches. catalog.jsonSchema({ strict: true }) is the structured-output shape — but elements is a map, so strict JSON Schema cannot list keys; that is why a
  generate loop that only dumps jsonSchema({ strict: true }) cannot autogenerate the whole GUI by itself.

  2. Blob / plugin catalog (what exists on the bus)

  Each plugin’s Rust state struct is its PluginSchema (schemars → seal). Live artifacts:

  ┌───────────────┬─────────────────────────────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
  │ Store         │ Path                                            │ Meaning                                           │
  ├───────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ Sealed schema │ /dev/shm/opdbus/plugin-blobs/<id>.<hash16>.blob │ Immutable contract + schema_hash                  │
  ├───────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ Manifest      │ plugin-blobs/.manifest.json                     │ catalog_hash, generation                          │
  ├───────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ Present state │ /dev/shm/opdbus/state/<id>.json                 │ Live values                                       │
  ├───────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ HTTP          │ GET /api/ui-model/plugin-schema/:plugin         │ Full schema + schema_hash + ui_projection + state │
  └───────────────┴─────────────────────────────────────────────────┴───────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

  Render source is schema_json in the blob, never gRPC reflection (reflection is methods-only and collapses types).

  ui_surfaces on a plugin (e.g. antigravity) are { path, name, schema }:

  • /antigravity → antigravity
  • /antigravity/chat → antigravity.chat
  • plus safety / usage / auth

  That is the page list for one fat schema, not a variant enum invented in the SPA.

  project_schema_ui then remaps every field’s OSCAL subid category (exp/obs/mut/…) to a role (surface, display-value, text-control, record-editor, …). Roles are presentation semantics. They are not
  catalog component names. Mapping role → card / stateValue / pluginState is the missing client step; without it, a catalog-gated renderer is handed names it does not know and draws nothing.

  3. The stream (how live data arrives)

  StateSync (operation.v1.StateSync.Subscribe on the bridge, same-origin via op-web :8080 → :8090). Subscribe with initial state + schema frames.

  Each frame is a plugin object:

  • SCHEMA_MIGRATION → /schemas/<id>, /schemaHashes/<id>
  • value → /plugins/<id> (and /plugins/<id>/<member>)
  • catalog identity → /catalogHash
  • index of seen plugins → /pluginIndex

  The SPA store is json-render createStateStore (uiStore). Specs bind with $state / stateValue / pluginState / named stream objects (type: "antigravity" reads /plugins/antigravity).

  Identity headers (x-ghostbridge-footprint / trace-id) come from pairing / /api/identity/sled. No identity → the stream never starts.

  Chat is a second stream, not StateSync: op_chat.chat.ChatService.Send. Tokens land in /streams/<streamId>/messages. The catalog host is antigravityChatContainer + chatMessage with repeat.statePath.
  Provider/model come from tched_router.selected_provider / selected_model. That is the antigravity.chat surface, not OpenAI useChat and not :50051.

  4. How catalog and stream meet

  PluginSchema (blob)     →  fields, methods, ui_surfaces, schema_hash
          │
          ├─ StateSync    →  uiStore /plugins/<id>     (live values)
          ├─ ui_projection→  roles per subid           (how to present)
          └─ component catalog → Spec.type must be here (how to paint)
  Spec = composition of catalog types
       + bindings into /plugins, /streams, /shell, /connected

  A stream object in the catalog (STREAM_PLUGIN_IDS → camelCase type) is just a card over /plugins/<id>. Layout primitives compose those objects. Chat is the exception that needs its own catalog types
  because the data plane is ChatService, not a StateSync member.

  Shell route state (/shell/route) is synced from the router so nav highlighting is declarative.

  5. Autogenerating the whole GUI (the real loop)

  Not “one prompt → one spec in a textarea.” The fill loop is op-gallery-gen:

  1. Assemble all sealed schemas + catalog.prompt.md (same bytes as the guard).
  2. Model (via tched_router / ZeroClaw, not a hardcoded gpt-4o) emits JSONL patches (that is what Catalog.prompt() specifies).
  3. spec_stream::assemble folds patches into a spec; CatalogGuard admits only catalog types.
  4. Operator reviews in gallery, promotes into catalog, pinned to schema_hash.
  5. Nav/pages should come from ui_surfaces + admitted specs, not a hand list of React routes.

  Until role → catalog-type mapping is implemented, projections exist and stream values exist, but the sanctioned renderer still has nothing it can paint for a generated plugin page.

  One-line model: the component catalog is the paint vocabulary; the blob catalog is the typed world; the stream is the live binding. A GUI is a spec that only uses the first, only names objects from
  the second, and only reads values from the third.
