To hook up your live message updates directly into that antigravity UI, you need to append incoming text chunks to your state array in real time. Because you are using a Vercel-oriented stack (json-render), the cleanest way to drive this interface is by using the Vercel AI SDK (useChat) alongside your layout state.
Here is how you wire up the live token parsing loop.
1. Bind the Live Stream Hook to Framework State
You can capture the streaming updates inside a React useEffect loop, updating the json-render local state slice on every delta frame.
typescript
import { useChat } from 'ai/react';
import { useJSONUI, Renderer } from '@json-render/react';
import { useEffect } from 'react';

export function AntigravityLiveTerminal() {
  // 1. Initialize the standard Vercel AI stream ingestion engine
  const { messages, input, handleInputChange, handleSubmit } = useChat({
    api: '/api/chat/antigravity',
  });

  // 2. Grab the local framework state manipulator 
  const { updateState } = useJSONUI();

  // 3. Sync incoming tokens seamlessly into the catalog data-binding path
  useEffect(() => {
    updateState('/streams/stream_antigravity_01/messages', messages);
  }, [messages, updateState]);

  // Load the structural layout layout declaration from Step 3
  const uiSpec = getAntigravityChatSpec();

  return (
    <div className="space-y-4">
      {/* Renders the conversational card blocks entirely out of the catalog config */}
      <Renderer spec={uiSpec} />

      {/* Manual message injection footer */}
      <form onSubmit={handleSubmit} className="flex gap-2">
        <input
          value={input}
          onChange={handleInputChange}
          placeholder="Send antigravity vector adjust order..."
          className="flex-1 bg-zinc-900 border border-zinc-800 text-white rounded p-2 text-sm focus:outline-none focus:ring-1 focus:ring-blue-500"
        />
        <button type="submit" className="bg-blue-600 px-4 py-2 text-sm text-white rounded">
          Send
        </button>
      </form>
    </div>
  );
}
Use code with caution.
2. Configure the Edge API Route (app/api/chat/antigravity/route.ts)
On the backend, handle the incoming text sequence using an Edge runtime function that sends an event stream back down the pipe.
typescript
import { openai } from '@ai-sdk/openai';
import { streamText } from 'ai';

export const runtime = 'edge';

export async function POST(req: Request) {
  const { messages } = await req.json();

  const result = await streamText({
    model: openai('gpt-4o'),
    system: 'You are the Antigravity Stream Operator. Keep responses concise and clinical.',
    messages,
  });

