To get the LLM to automatically create the UI from available components in your event stream, you have to pass the Catalog definition into the LLM's system prompt as a rigid JSON schema or TypeScript definition. This acts as a set of guardrails.
Instead of generating raw text, the model processes the user's natural language input and outputs structural JSONL (JSON Lines) Patches matching RFC6902, which add or modify components in real-time.
The production implementation uses the Vercel AI SDK alongside json-render:
1. Build the AI Schema Prompt from your Catalog
To ensure the LLM only picks components that actually exist in your catalog, stringify the catalog schema directly into your system prompt.
